      "content": "To determine the significance, you'll need to employ regression analysis, such as logistic or Poisson regression, where your dependent variable is theft risk and your independent variables include measures of ethnic composition and diversity. Check the p-values associated with these demographic features within your model output; a low p-value generally indicates a statistically significant relationship. Furthermore, consider including interaction terms to see if the effect of diversity changes depending on the baseline theft rate.",
