      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is a common, yet heavily debated, finding in some raw datasets that demographic markers correlate with crime rates, but this correlation is often spurious and reflects underlying socio-economic factors rather than inherent group behavior. Relying solely on ethnicity as a predictor in actuarial models is highly problematic due to bias and ethical concerns. Instead, focus your model on controllable risk factors like poverty levels, housing density, unemployment rates, and neighborhood resource availability, as these have established links to property crime.",
